<title>USA: Boyd Bros raising truck drivers' pay.</title>
<headline>Boyd Bros raising truck drivers' pay.</headline>
<dateline>CLAYTON, Ala. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boyd Bros Transportation Co Inc, a large flatbed carrier, said it raised its pay scale in an effort to recruit experienced drivers.</p>
<p>The company said it will pay drivers with one-year experience up to $0.32 a mile, effective February 11, up from $0.30 a mile currently.</p>
<p>The new pay scale for experienced drivers will top out at $0.36 a mile, up from $0.35 previously.</p>
<p>A Boyd Bros spokesman said no material impact on earnings is expected in the short-term, although the company may reap some savings on recruiting and training drivers over a longer term.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
